--TEST--
A string converted while the program runs takes `@key` and `@value` after an array, as a written path does, with `as propertyPath<T>` and in the holes of `as string<propertyPath<T>>`; a misplaced step gives `null` with `as ?propertyPath<T>` and throws with `as propertyPath<T>`, and the error says what the compiler says — `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A path from a string can take `@key` and `@value` after an array.
// A step in the wrong place throws an error that names it.
class Author {
    public string $name = "Ada";
    public string $value = "high";
}

class Book {
    public array<string> $tags = [];
    public array<Author> $authors = [];
    public array<array<Author>> $grid = [];
    public ?array<Author> $editors = null;
    public int $pages = 1;
}

class Check {
    public static function path(string $text): void {
        ?propertyPath<Book> $maybe = $text as ?propertyPath<Book>;
        if ($maybe == null) {
            echo "null: ";
        }
        try {
            propertyPath<Book> $path = $text as propertyPath<Book>;
            echo "valid: ", $path as string, "\n";
        } catch (Throwable $e) {
            echo $e->message, "\n";
        }
    }

    public static function holes(string $text): void {
        try {
            string<propertyPath<Book>> $c = $text as string<propertyPath<Book>>;
            echo "valid: ", $c as string, "\n";
        } catch (Throwable $e) {
            echo $e->message, "\n";
        }
    }
}

// These paths are valid.
Check::path("tags.@key");
Check::path("tags.@value");
Check::path("authors.@value.name");
Check::path("authors.name");
Check::path("authors.value");
Check::path("grid.@value.@key");
Check::path("grid.@value.@value.name");
Check::path("grid.@value.name");
Check::path("editors.@key");
Check::path("editors.name");
Check::holes("{tags.@value} = 'new' AND {authors.@key} < 3");
Check::holes("{grid.@value.@value.name} <> ''");

// These paths are not valid.
Check::path("pages.@key");
Check::path("@value");
Check::path("authors.@key.name");
Check::path("authors.@index");
Check::path("tags.@value.name");
Check::path("tags.@value.@key");
Check::path("authors.@value.name.@value");
Check::path("tags.name");
Check::path("authors.title");
Check::holes("{authors.@key.name} = 1");
Check::holes("{tags.name} = 1");
// covers: lang:types/property-paths
--EXPECT--
valid: tags.@key
valid: tags.@value
valid: authors.@value.name
valid: authors.name
valid: authors.value
valid: grid.@value.@key
valid: grid.@value.@value.name
valid: grid.@value.name
valid: editors.@key
valid: editors.name
valid: {tags.@value} = 'new' AND {authors.@key} < 3
valid: {grid.@value.@value.name} <> ''
null: a `string` of 10 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `$pages` is not an array, so the path cannot take `@key` after it
null: a `string` of 6 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `Book` is a class, so the path cannot start with `@value`
null: a `string` of 17 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `@key` ends a property path, so nothing can follow it
null: a `string` of 14 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `@index` is not a step: an array's steps are `@key` and `@value`
null: a `string` of 16 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `@value` of `array<string>` is not an object, so the path cannot continue after it
null: a `string` of 16 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `@value` is not an array, so the path cannot take `@key` after it
null: a `string` of 26 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `$name` is not an array, so the path cannot take `@value` after it
null: a `string` of 9 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `array<string>` has no public property `$name`
null: a `string` of 13 bytes is not a property path of `Book`: `Author` has no public property `$title`
a `string` of 23 bytes is not a string with holes of `Book`: in the hole `{authors.@key.name}`, `@key` ends a property path, so nothing can follow it
a `string` of 15 bytes is not a string with holes of `Book`: in the hole `{tags.name}`, `array<string>` has no public property `$name`
